Run garbage collections only at the top of the engine's event loop.

The conservative stack scan reads linear memory, but wasm keeps C++ locals in
the engine's own locals, out of its reach: a collection started in the middle
of a call (an allocation slow path, a DeferGC release, a safepoint) freed cells
still in use. Requests made there are recorded instead, and the embedder runs
them when no native frame holds cells.

